/*!
    \page about.html
    \title About and Version Information
    \previouspage Troubleshooting

    \section1 Application version

    The application version is shown in the \e{Help > About} dialog, together with build
    and toolchain information and the license notices. The version comes from a single
    source of truth (the product metadata), which also drives the installer and the
    Windows executable metadata (\l AppInfo).

    \section1 Documentation version

    This documentation is generated together with the application from the same source
    tree and version, so the help you open from the program matches the program you are
    running. The version below is substituted at build time.

    \list
        \li Documentation version: \b {\appversion}
    \endlist

    \section1 Licensing

    The application is distributed under its stated license, and it bundles third-party
    components under their own licenses. The full texts and notices are available in the
    \e{Help > About} dialog and in the license files shipped next to the program.

    \section1 Feedback

    When reporting an issue, please include the application version above and, where
    relevant, the log excerpt described in \l {Troubleshooting}.
*/
